' ============================================================================
' 52 TL admission theories: the three points of the theory seam.
'
' Source of Figure TL18 in ../tensor-logic/integration.md (section 6). The
' figure restates that section, tensor-logic/gslt.md section 10, decision 74
' and the theory seam (theory-seam.md, sections 7 to 9). It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. At creation, the factory resolves the identity of the TensorCheck
'      theory and stores it as compact bytes in the config of the space.
'   2. At a send, each value is checked before any staging, and a verdict
'      other than Proven aborts the deploy.
'   3. At a match, each stored datum is checked again in the COMM, and a
'      verdict other than Proven makes it ineligible.
'   4. A theory check adds no phlo (rule TH-8).
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 52-tl-admission.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 52-tl-admission
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor $rrs_relation
  LifeLineBorderColor $rrs_relation
  ParticipantBorderColor $rrs_relation
  ActorBorderColor $rrs_relation
  GroupBorderColor $rrs_relation
  DividerBorderColor $rrs_relation
  DividerBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
}
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title TL admission theories (integration 6)
autonumber

participant "Deploy" as DEPLOY $rrs_host
participant "Factory and\nspace agent" as AGENT $rrs_agent
participant "Theory seam" as SEAM $rrs_checker
participant "TL engine" as ENGINE $rrs_tl_engine
database "RSpace" as RSPACE $rrs_storage

== At creation ==
DEPLOY -> AGENT : Factory!?(free TensorCheck(tl,\n  tl:Check{ v : [D] in { min[d](v[d] >= 0) } }, 64))
AGENT -> SEAM : resolve the identity of the theory
SEAM -> ENGINE : normalize the check term, and hash its NF
ENGINE --> SEAM : <latex>h = \mathrm{Blake2b256}(\mathrm{bytes}(\mathrm{NF}))</latex>
SEAM --> AGENT : the identity, with theoremId "tl:check:" || hex(h)
AGENT -> RSPACE : the config C(sid) with the compact identity bytes,\nand the content record <latex>\mathtt{E0} \Vert \mathtt{T} \Vert h</latex> (open question K8)

== At a send ==
DEPLOY -> AGENT : space!(v)
AGENT -> RSPACE : read the identity from the config
AGENT -> ENGINE : check v
alt ok = 1
  ENGINE --> AGENT : Proven
  AGENT -> RSPACE : stage and commit the send
else ok = 0, a value that does not decode, a limit or PrecisionExhausted
  ENGINE --> AGENT : Refuted or Undetermined
  AGENT -[$rrs_fail]-> DEPLOY : abort before any staging (fail closed)
end

== At a match ==
AGENT -> ENGINE : check each stored datum again, in the COMM
alt Proven
  AGENT -> RSPACE : the datum stays eligible
else Refuted or Undetermined
  AGENT -> AGENT : the datum is ineligible, as after a guard rejection
end
note over SEAM, ENGINE
  A check is a pure function of the identity and the value,
  so play, replay and a later attach give the same verdicts.
end note

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_host>      | the deploy |
|<$rrs_agent>     | the factory and the space agent |
|<$rrs_checker>   | the theory seam and the TL engine |
|<$rrs_storage>   | consensus state in RSpace |
endlegend
@enduml
